1
00:00:00,135 --> 00:00:03,990
3 hours, then 2: a day
is as long as a movie.

2
00:00:04,260 --> 00:00:05,955
At a 3 hour day,

3
00:00:05,955 --> 00:00:09,275
the Sun crosses the sky
in just 90 minutes.

4
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:13,235
It slides its own
width every 16 seconds.

5
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:15,875
The ground now
moves at over

6
00:00:15,875 --> 00:00:18,880
13,000 km/h.

7
00:00:19,187 --> 00:00:21,547
You weigh 22% less.

8
00:00:21,853 --> 00:00:24,498
70 kg
feels like 55.

9
00:00:24,793 --> 00:00:27,723
At 2 hours, you weigh
half of what you did.

10
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:31,180
The same jump that lifts
you half a meter

11
00:00:31,180 --> 00:00:34,020
today would now lift
you about a meter.

12
00:00:34,718 --> 00:00:37,468
20,000 km/h;

13
00:00:37,498 --> 00:00:40,643
the Sun crosses
the whole sky in an hour.

14
00:00:41,293 --> 00:00:43,493
Every object
near the equator

15
00:00:43,493 --> 00:00:46,138
is half as heavy
as it should be.

16
00:00:46,320 --> 00:00:49,515
Buildings,
bridges and oceans are all

17
00:00:49,515 --> 00:00:52,550
being asked to hold
on with half the force.

18
00:00:52,818 --> 00:00:54,073
Hang on.

19
00:00:54,178 --> 00:00:56,998
If you're enjoying this,
tap like and follow.

20
00:00:57,208 --> 00:00:58,933
Okay, back to the math.

21
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:02,535
And at an hour and a half,
you are almost weightless.

22
00:01:03,018 --> 00:01:04,893
Part 7 of 8.
